<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6700] Node considered as failed can cause failure of others nodes</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6700</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Node considered as failed can cause failure of others nodes in cluster. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is an issue in TcpDiscoveryAbstractMessage.failedNodes processing, if message is received from node considered as failed, then failedNodes should be ignored.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible scenario:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;there are 4 nodes (1 -&amp;gt; 2 -&amp;gt; 3 -&amp;gt; 4)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;node 3 temporary lost connection with others&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;node 2 considers 3 as failed, node failed event is fired for 3&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;node 3 considers 4 as failed, adds 4 in nodeFailedList, then it restores connection with 1 and currently 1 will process nodeFailedList from 3 (even if 3 is already considered as failed)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
                <environment></environment>
